{"step_index":1197,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:38:24Z","thinking":"**Examining Vertex Labeling Cases**\n\nAnalyzing the problem's mathematical structure to identify the relevant cases for vertices labeled with the value 2, denoted as  $V_2 = \\{v \\in V \\mid f(v) = 2\\}$. Considering the scenario where $|V_2| = 0$, meaning no vertex has a label of 2.\n\nIn this initial case, because every vertex must have $f(v) \\ge 1$, the total number of vertices $|V|$ is less than or equal to the romanWeight of the function, which could be useful. The aim is to apply the relation by `radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_card_le` which suggests $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$.\n\n\n**Exploring Cases and Hypotheses**\n\nConsidering the case where $|V_2| = 1$, the relation `radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_unique_two` directly implies  $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$. For $|V_2| \\ge 2$, deduce that $\\text{romanWeight}(f) \\ge 4$.\n\nExploring the general relationship between radius and romanWeight. Acknowledging the conjecture that $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le \\text{romanDominationNumber}(G)$, which is the minimal Roman weight. However, I am now focused on whether  $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$ holds for *every* Roman dominating function $f$.\n\n\n**Re-evaluating the central inequality**\n\nRecognizing that $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le \\text{romanDominationNumber}(G)$ implies $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$ for *all* Roman dominating functions, because the roman domination number is the minimum Roman weight. Initially doubted this conclusion but it appears sound due to the minimum property.\n\nThe lemma `le_romanDominationNumber` is relevant; it states that if a value *k* is less than or equal to the Roman weight of *every* Roman dominating function, then *k* is less than or equal to the Roman domination number. This seems related to the central problem.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cat scratch_goal.lean scratch_rdn.lean\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Viewing scratch files\"","toolSummary":"\"View scratch_goal.lean and scratch_rdn.lean\""}}]}
{"step_index":1198,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:38:30Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:38:30+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:38:30+02:00\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\nimport Mathlib\r\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\r\n\r\nopen SimpleGraph\r\nopen GraphCalc\r\n\r\n-- We have the lemmas from Challenge_e20263a9.lean\r\nimport Mathlib\r\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\r\n\r\nopen SimpleGraph\r\nopen GraphCalc\r\n\r\nlemma two_le_romanWeight {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\r\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\r\n    (hnt : GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G) (f : V → Fin 3)\r\n    (hf : GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G f) :\r\n    2 ≤ GraphCalc.romanWeight f := by\r\n  unfold GraphCalc.romanWeight\r\n  unfold GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass at hnt\r\n  unfold GraphCalc.order at hnt\r\n  by_contra hc\r\n  have h_le1 : ∑ v : V, (f v : ℕ) ≤ 1 := by omega\r\n  have h_no2 : ∀ v : V, (f v : ℕ) ≠ 2 := by\r\n    intro v hv\r\n    have h_mem := Finset.single_le_sum (fun u _ => Nat.zero_le (f u : ℕ)) (Finset.mem_univ v)\r\n    rw [hv] at h_mem\r\n    omega\r\n  have h_no0 : ∀ v : V, (f v : ℕ) ≠ 0 := by\r\n    intro v hv\r\n    have h_f0 : f v = 0 := by\r\n      ext\r\n      exact hv\r\n    obtain ⟨u, _, hu2⟩ := hf v h_f0\r\n    have hu2_nat : (f u : ℕ) = 2 := by\r\n      rw [hu2]\r\n      rfl\r\n    exact h_no2 u hu2_nat\r\n  have h_ge1 : ∀ v : V, 1 ≤ (f v : ℕ) := by\r\n    intro v\r\n    have h0 := h_no0 v\r\n    omega\r\n  have h_sum_ge : ∑ v : V, 1 ≤ ∑ v : V, (f v : ℕ) :=\r\n    Finset.sum_le_sum (fun v _ => h_ge1 v)\r\n  rw [Finset.sum_const, nsmul_eq_mul, mul_one] at h_sum_ge\r\n  rw [Finset.card_univ] at h_sum_ge\r\n  have h2 : 2 ≤ ∑ v : V, (f v : ℕ) := hnt.trans h_sum_ge\r\n  omega\r\n\r\nlemma two_le_romanDominationNumber {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\r\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\r\n    (hnt : GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G) :\r\n    2 ≤ GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber G := by\r\n  unfold GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber\r\n  let S := (Finset.univ.filter (GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G)).image GraphCalc.romanWeight\r\n  have hconst : (fun _ : V => (2 : Fin 3)) ∈ Finset.univ.filter (GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G) := by\r\n    rw [Finset.mem_filter]\r\n    refine ⟨Finset.mem_univ _, ?_⟩\r\n    intro v hv\r\n    have h20 : (2 : Fin 3) ≠ 0 := by decide\r\n    exact False.elim (h20 hv)\r\n  have hSne : S.Nonempty := by\r\n    use GraphCalc.romanWeight (fun _ : V => (2 : Fin 3))\r\n    apply Finset.mem_image_of_mem\r\n    exact hconst\r\n  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := Finset.min_of_nonempty hSne\r\n  rw [hm]\r\n  dsimp\r\n  have hmem : m ∈ S := Finset.mem_of_min hm\r\n  rw [Finset.mem_image] at hmem\r\n  obtain ⟨f, hf, rfl⟩ := hmem\r\n  rw [Finset.mem_filter] at hf\r\n  exact two_le_romanWeight G hnt f hf.2\r\n\r\n\n"}
